WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.675
Coding Exercise 4 tests whether you can encode a
policy that includes

00:00:03.688 --> 00:00:09.100
missing status The wording is not definitely Paid
That means a NULL

00:00:09.125 --> 00:00:13.688
status should remain in the result for review
Ordinary not-equal does not

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.375
satisfy that policy because NULL compared with Paid
becomes UNKNOWN and is

00:00:17.388 --> 00:00:22.150
filtered out Use IS DISTINCT FROM to get a definite
Boolean result

00:00:23.025 --> 00:00:27.812
After running you should see six billing rows The
missing status record

00:00:27.838 --> 00:00:32.562
is an important part of the expected result This
short exercise captures

00:00:32.588 --> 00:00:36.088
an important distinction between a known non-Paid
status and a status that

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.562
is simply not known to be Paid
